      "body": "### Summary\n\n`mx.gather_mm(..., lhs_indices=None, sorted_indices=True)` silently returns **wrong results** when the `a` operand is a non-contiguous view created by inserting an axis (`x[:, None, :]`). No error is raised; the output is catastrophically wrong (not a rounding difference). The same call with `sorted_indices=False`, or with an explicit `lhs_indices`, or with a natively-3D `a`, is correct.\n\n### Repro (mlx 0.31.2, M3 Ultra)\n\n```python\nimport mlx.core as mx\nimport numpy as np\n\nE, ROWS, K, N = 4, 3, 256, 64\nR = E * ROWS\nidx = mx.array(np.repeat(np.arange(E, dtype=np.uint32), ROWS))   # sorted\n\nfor tag, build in ((\"3D direct\", lambda: mx.random.normal((R, 1, K))),\n                   (\"2D + [:, None, :]\", lambda: mx.random.normal((R, K))[:, None, :])):\n    mx.random.seed(0)\n    W = mx.random.normal((E, K, N))\n    x = build()\n    ref = mx.stack([x[r, 0] @ W[int(idx[r])] for r in range(R)])\n    y = mx.gather_mm(x, W, lhs_indices=None, rhs_indices=idx, sorted_indices=True)[:, 0, :]\n    print(f\"{tag}: max|delta| = {mx.abs(y - ref).max().item():.4f}\")\n```\n\n```\n3D direct: max|delta| = 0.0000\n2D + [:, None, :]: max|delta| = 80.1779      # silently wrong\n```\n\nDeterministic across seeds (80.2 / 76.5 / 84.9 for seeds 0/1/2) and across float32 / float16 / bfloat16. Correct in all three of these variants:\n\n- `sorted_indices=False` (same view) \u2192 0.0\n- `lhs_indices=mx.arange(R, dtype=mx.uint32)` + `sorted_indices=True` (same view) \u2192 0.0\n- natively-3D `a` + `lhs_indices=None` + `sorted_indices=True` \u2192 0.0\n\nSo the sorted fast path appears to assume a contiguous/row-major `a` layout when `lhs_indices` is None, and reads the wrong rows otherwise.\n\n### Why this is worth fixing rather than documenting\n\n`x[:, None, :]` is the idiomatic way to shape a `[rows, K]` activation matrix for `gather_mm` in a MoE forward \u2014 it is exactly what our 2.8T-parameter MoE port does when it groups tokens by expert:\n\n```python\nx_c = xf[tok_sorted[s0:s1]][:, None, :]        # the view\ny   = mx.gather_mm(x_c, W, lhs_indices=None, rhs_indices=slot, ...)\n```\n\nOur code happens to pass `sorted_indices=False`, so it is correct today \u2014 but the rows *are* sorted, so flipping that flag to True is the obvious \"free speedup\" a reader would try, and it would silently corrupt every expert output with no error, no NaN, and plausible-looking magnitudes. Quantized `gather_qmm` with the identical argument pattern is correct, which makes the inconsistency easy to trust into a bug.\n\nI am happy to test a fix against a large real MoE workload (2.8T model, 896 experts, top-16) on M3 Ultra if that helps.\n\n### Suggested minimum\n\nEither fix the layout handling on the sorted path, or raise when `sorted_indices=True` is combined with a non-contiguous `a` and `lhs_indices=None`.\n",
